    "description": "<p><strong>Context</strong>\nAdding a new referrer from a sign-up currently takes an extra click/screen, and forces a record-type selection step that&#039;s likely unnecessary given referrers are a known, single use case here.</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><ul><li><p>When a user clicks &quot;Add New Account&quot; to create a new referrer from a sign-up, take them directly into the referrer-creation screen instead of an intermediate screen requiring a second click.</p></li><li><p>Investigate whether the Record Type selection screen (shown when creating a referrer via the lookup field) can be skipped or defaulted to &quot;Referrer&quot; without a large rebuild. This was looked into before — an earlier investigation suggested it might require a large overhaul rather than a simple setting; re-confirm current effort estimate.</p></li><li><p>At minimum, if skipping the screen entirely isn&#039;t feasible without major rework, default the Record Type selection to &quot;Referrer&quot; so users aren&#039;t creating the wrong type by mistake.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Constraints / Dependencies</strong>\nRelated to an existing open bug Kobi assigned to Cedrick the same day (New Referrer on the Log Signup screen flow pointing to the incorrect layout vs. the Referrer edit/create screens) — worth coordinating so both aren&#039;t solved in conflicting ways.</p><p><strong>Source</strong>\nFathom — WagerTech &lt;&gt; Jumpr Weekly Sync, 09/23/2026 (https://fathom.video/calls/831090060) — Emily Vandenberg ~35:44–37:12, Kobi Kunasekaran ~36:12–36:48. Also Taryn&#039;s notes, Sign-ups &gt; &quot;New referrer → the record type selection isn&#039;t easily customized — or just default to referrer.&quot;</p>",
